From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:36:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Show the ME state in setup and SMBIOS

On the W541 the ME is reduced by me_cleaner -S and its HECI interface
is hidden from the OS by default (me_disable), so nothing but the boot
log shows what the ME did, and the log has only the decoded fields.
The M920x reads the registers when the tables are written, but here
intel_me_finalize() hides 00:16.0 at BS_POST_DEVICE, before SMBIOS and
the setup menu exist: a read then would always fail.

me_status.c therefore takes a snapshot of HFS1-6 (0x40, 0x48, 0x60,
0x64, 0x68 and 0x6c, the six words that Linux reads on Lynx Point) on
entry to BS_DEV_INIT, where intel_me_path() logs them too, with one
debug line. It sends no HECI message, skips an S3 resume and a device
that is off or hidden, and reads me_disable as intel_me_finalize() does.

The summary follows HFS2 first. A progress phase of BUP with state
0x0a (checking the straps) and no error is "Disabled (AltMeDisable,
BUP)", whatever the operation mode: ME 7 and 8 report mode 2 for it
(d7e0cb93ae), which is not verified for ME 9, and a stopped ME must not
be called enabled. Any other stop in BUP is "Stopped in BUP (state
0xNN)". Only then the operation mode gives the texts of the M920x.

- General > About this ThinkPad gets a read-only "Management Engine"
  line with that summary. Its help has the registers, the working
  state, operation state and mode, error code, progress phase and
  state, the AltMeDisable meaning, whether HECI is hidden, and which
  updates write the ME region.
- SMBIOS type 11 gets "ME: <summary>" and "ME HFSTS: " with the six
  words, at most 64 characters each, through the root device's
  get_smbios_strings. They join the structure of the H8 EC string,
  before it: no new structure, and thinkpad_acpi scans every string.

The T440p shares the code and keeps its menu and SMBIOS: the line is
suppressed and no snapshot is taken there. The help of me_disable no
longer says that the ME keeps running, which a stopped ME does not.

TEST=Built me_status.c on the host against stubbed registers: HFS
00020191 and HFS2 100A0000 (an X220 with me_cleaner), and the same with
mode 0, give "Disabled (AltMeDisable, BUP)" and a help text of 550 of
639 bytes; a BUP stop with error 3 gives "Stopped in BUP (state 0x18)";
the other modes, a hidden device and a 63-character HFSTS string as
expected. Host syntax check of the changed files with the W541 mrc and
nri configs and a T440p one; tools/cfr-dump.sh: the W541 menu is valid
with info_me in About. For the W541 hardware test: the line and its
help, the "ME: HFSTS1-6" log line with the same words, both strings in
dmidecode -t 11 next to the EC string and the same SMBIOS handle count;
after a warm reboot with HECI hidden the registers are still there;
with HECI on, setpci -s 00:16.0 40.l 48.l 60.l 64.l 68.l 6c.l gives
the same words. On nri, compare a cold boot and a warm reboot: what
"ME: Checking whether CPU was replaced..." prints (not replaced,
replaced, or timed out) and whether "CPU was replaced, forcing a cold
boot" follows, which with the ME stopped in BUP would train the memory
again at every boot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/Makefile.mk |   1 +
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c       |  18 +++
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/mainboard.c |  23 +++
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/me_status.c | 179 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/me_status.h |  32 ++++
 src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/cfr.h    |   2 +-
 6 files changed, 254 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/me_status.c
 create mode 100644 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/me_status.h

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/Makefile.mk b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/Makefile.mk
index f96e1b8923..4334b65261 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/Makefile.mk
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/Makefile.mk
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@ romstage-y += variants/$(VARIANT_DIR)/gpio.c
 romstage-y += variants/$(VARIANT_DIR)/romstage.c
 
 ramstage-y += mainboard.c
+ramstage-y += me_status.c
 ramstage-$(CONFIG_DRIVERS_OPTION_CFR) += cfr.c
 
 ramstage-$(CONFIG_MAINBOARD_USE_LIBGFXINIT) += variants/$(VARIANT_DIR)/gma-mainboard.ads
diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
index 83760de4b8..4395304b8a 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 
+#include "me_status.h"
 #include "setup_options.h"
 
 /*
@@ -189,6 +190,22 @@ static const struct sm_object info_ec_firmware = SM_DECLARE_VARCHAR({
 	.default_value	= "Unknown",
 }, WITH_CALLBACK(update_ec_firmware));
 
+/* What ramstage read of the ME at this boot (me_status.c), on the W541 */
+static void update_me(struct sm_object *new)
+{
+	new->sm_varchar.default_value = mainboard_me_summary();
+	new->sm_varchar.ui_helptext = mainboard_me_details();
+}
+
+static const struct sm_object info_me = SM_DECLARE_VARCHAR({
+	.flags		= CFR_OPTFLAG_READONLY | CFR_OPTFLAG_VOLATILE |
+			  (CONFIG(BOARD_LENOVO_THINKPAD_W541) ? 0 : CFR_OPTFLAG_SUPPRESS),
+	.opt_name	= "info_me",
+	.ui_name	= "Management Engine",
+	.ui_helptext	= "The state of the Intel ME at this boot.",
+	.default_value	= "Unknown",
+}, WITH_CALLBACK(update_me));
+
 static const struct sm_object general_about = SM_DECLARE_FORM({
 	.ui_name	= "About this ThinkPad",
 	.obj_list	= (const struct sm_object *[]) {
@@ -202,6 +219,7 @@ static const struct sm_object general_about = SM_DECLARE_FORM({
 		&info_memory_profile,
 		&info_firmware,
 		&info_ec_firmware,
+		&info_me,
 		NULL
 	},
 });
diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/mainboard.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/mainboard.c
index b4d66ef738..4e8ad6ba68 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/mainboard.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/mainboard.c
@@ -11,8 +11,10 @@
 #include <option.h>
 #include <smbios.h>
 #include <southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/chip.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
 #include <string.h>
 
+#include "me_status.h"
 #include "setup_options.h"
 
 /* Battery charge thresholds in EC RAM, as in thinkpad_bat_thresholds_b0.asl */
@@ -126,9 +128,30 @@ static void set_sata_ports(void)
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * W541: the ME state for the OS (dmidecode -t 11, tools/update.py status),
+ * which has no HECI to ask with me_disable on. At most 64 characters each.
+ */
+static void mainboard_smbios_strings(struct device *dev, struct smbios_type11 *t)
+{
+	const struct mb_me_status *me = mainboard_me_status();
+	char text[65];
+
+	snprintf(text, sizeof(text), "ME: %s", mainboard_me_summary());
+	t->count = smbios_add_string(t->eos, text);
+	if (!me->valid)
+		return;
+	snprintf(text, sizeof(text), "ME HFSTS: %08X %08X %08X %08X %08X %08X",
+		 me->hfs[0], me->hfs[1], me->hfs[2], me->hfs[3], me->hfs[4], me->hfs[5]);
+	t->count = smbios_add_string(t->eos, text);
+}
+
 static void mainboard_enable(struct device *dev)
 {
+	/* dev is the root device, whose operations each board may extend */
 	dev->ops->acpi_fill_ssdt = mainboard_fill_ssdt;
+	if (CONFIG(BOARD_LENOVO_THINKPAD_W541) && CONFIG(GENERATE_SMBIOS_TABLES))
+		dev->ops->get_smbios_strings = mainboard_smbios_strings;
 
 	if (CONFIG(BOARD_LENOVO_THINKPAD_W541))
 		set_sata_ports();
diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/me_status.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/me_status.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..c83407d3e3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/me_status.c
@@ -0,0 +1,179 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only */
+
+#include <acpi/acpi.h>
+#include <bootstate.h>
+#include <commonlib/helpers.h>
+#include <console/console.h>
+#include <device/device.h>
+#include <device/pci_def.h>
+#include <device/pci_ops.h>
+#include <option.h>
+#include <southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/me.h>
+#include <stdarg.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <string.h>
+
+#include "me_status.h"
+
+/* The other status registers that Linux reads on Lynx Point (PCI_CFG_HFS_3, _4 and _6) */
+#define PCI_ME_HFS3	0x60
+#define PCI_ME_HFS4	0x64
+#define PCI_ME_HFS6	0x6c
+
+/*
+ * The registers that intel_me_path() logs at BS_DEV_INIT, read on its entry:
+ * with me_disable, intel_me_finalize() hides HECI at BS_POST_DEVICE, before
+ * SMBIOS and the setup menu are written. No HECI message, which a stopped ME
+ * would not answer. Only on the W541: the T440p keeps its setup and SMBIOS.
+ */
+const struct mb_me_status *mainboard_me_status(void)
+{
+	static const uint8_t hfs[] = {
+		PCI_ME_HFS, PCI_ME_HFS2, PCI_ME_HFS3, PCI_ME_HFS4, PCI_ME_HFS5, PCI_ME_HFS6,
+	};
+	static struct mb_me_status status;
+	static bool done;
+	const struct device *dev;
+
+	if (done)
+		return &status;
+	done = true;
+
+	if (!CONFIG(BOARD_LENOVO_THINKPAD_W541) || acpi_is_wakeup_s3())
+		return &status;
+
+	/* As intel_me_finalize() reads it */
+	status.me_disable = get_uint_option("me_disable", CONFIG(DISABLE_ME_PCI));
+
+	dev = pcidev_on_root(0x16, 0);
+	if (!dev || !dev->enabled || pci_read_config16(dev, PCI_VENDOR_ID) == 0xffff)
+		return &status;
+
+	for (size_t i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(hfs); i++)
+		status.hfs[i] = pci_read_config32(dev, hfs[i]);
+	status.valid = true;
+
+	printk(BIOS_DEBUG, "ME: HFSTS1-6: %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x\n",
+	       status.hfs[0], status.hfs[1], status.hfs[2],
+	       status.hfs[3], status.hfs[4], status.hfs[5]);
+
+	return &status;
+}
+
+static void me_status_snapshot(void *unused)
+{
+	mainboard_me_status();
+}
+
+BOOT_STATE_INIT_ENTRY(BS_DEV_INIT, BS_ON_ENTRY, me_status_snapshot, NULL);
+
+/*
+ * AltMeDisable, the strap that me_cleaner -S sets: the ME stops after its
+ * bring-up (BUP) once it has read the straps. ME 7 and 8 then report operation
+ * mode 2 (upstream commit d7e0cb93ae), not verified on ME 9, so the progress
+ * phase and state of HFS2 decide, whatever the mode: a stopped ME is never
+ * called enabled.
+ */
+static bool me_alt_disabled(union me_hfs hfs, union me_hfs2 hfs2)
+{
+	return hfs2.progress_code == ME_HFS2_PHASE_BUP &&
+	       hfs2.current_state == ME_HFS2_STATE_BUP_CHECK_STRAP &&
+	       hfs.error_code == ME_HFS_ERROR_NONE;
+}
+
+const char *mainboard_me_summary(void)
+{
+	static char text[32];
+	const struct mb_me_status *me = mainboard_me_status();
+	const union me_hfs hfs = { .raw = me->hfs[0] };
+	const union me_hfs2 hfs2 = { .raw = me->hfs[1] };
+
+	if (!me->valid)
+		return "Not available";
+
+	if (me_alt_disabled(hfs, hfs2))
+		return "Disabled (AltMeDisable, BUP)";
+
+	if (hfs2.progress_code == ME_HFS2_PHASE_BUP) {
+		snprintf(text, sizeof(text), "Stopped in BUP (state 0x%02x)",
+			 hfs2.current_state);
+		return text;
+	}
+
+	switch (hfs.operation_mode) {
+	case ME_HFS_MODE_NORMAL:
+		if (hfs.working_state == ME_HFS_CWS_NORMAL)
+			return "Enabled";
+		snprintf(text, sizeof(text), "Enabled, not ready (state %u)",
+			 hfs.working_state);
+		return text;
+	case ME_HFS_MODE_DIS:
+		return "Disabled (soft temporary disable)";
+	case ME_HFS_MODE_OVER_JMPR:
+		return "Security override (jumper)";
+	case ME_HFS_MODE_OVER_MEI:
+		return "Security override (HECI message)";
+	case ME_HFS_MODE_DEBUG:
+		return "Debug";
+	default:
+		snprintf(text, sizeof(text), "Mode %u", hfs.operation_mode);
+		return text;
+	}
+}
+
+/* Add to the text what fits */
+static void __printf(3, 4) text_add(char *text, size_t size, const char *fmt, ...)
+{
+	const size_t len = strnlen(text, size);
+	va_list args;
+
+	if (len + 1 >= size)
+		return;
+	va_start(args, fmt);
+	vsnprintf(text + len, size - len, fmt, args);
+	va_end(args);
+}
+
+const char *mainboard_me_details(void)
+{
+	static char text[640];
+	const struct mb_me_status *me = mainboard_me_status();
+	const union me_hfs hfs = { .raw = me->hfs[0] };
+	const union me_hfs2 hfs2 = { .raw = me->hfs[1] };
+
+	if (text[0])
+		return text;
+
+	if (!me->valid) {
+		text_add(text, sizeof(text),
+			 "The firmware could not read the ME at this boot: its HECI\n"
+			 "interface (00:16.0) was off or hidden.\n");
+	} else {
+		text_add(text, sizeof(text),
+			 "The Intel ME at this boot, from its status registers\n"
+			 "(HFS1-6):\n"
+			 "%08X %08X %08X %08X %08X %08X\n"
+			 "Working state %u, operation state %u, operation mode %u,\n"
+			 "error code %u; progress phase %u, state 0x%02x (HFS2).\n",
+			 me->hfs[0], me->hfs[1], me->hfs[2],
+			 me->hfs[3], me->hfs[4], me->hfs[5],
+			 hfs.working_state, hfs.operation_state, hfs.operation_mode,
+			 hfs.error_code, hfs2.progress_code, hfs2.current_state);
+		if (me_alt_disabled(hfs, hfs2))
+			text_add(text, sizeof(text),
+				 "Stopped after its bring-up (BUP) by the AltMeDisable\n"
+				 "strap of the flash descriptor (me_cleaner -S sets it).\n");
+		if (hfs.fpt_bad)
+			text_add(text, sizeof(text),
+				 "Its partition table in the flash is bad.\n");
+		text_add(text, sizeof(text), "HECI (00:16.0): %s.\n",
+			 me->me_disable ? "hidden from the OS at the end of the boot" :
+			 "visible to the OS");
+	}
+	text_add(text, sizeof(text),
+		 "Security > Management Engine only hides HECI. Capsules and\n"
+		 "flashrom --ifd -i bios do not write the ME region; the\n"
+		 "full-chip images write the one of this project.");
+
+	return text;
+}
diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/me_status.h b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/me_status.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..afe8431247
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/me_status.h
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only */
+
+#ifndef MAINBOARD_LENOVO_HASWELL_ME_STATUS_H
+#define MAINBOARD_LENOVO_HASWELL_ME_STATUS_H
+
+#include <types.h>
+
+/*
+ * The Intel ME at this boot, for the setup and SMBIOS (W541): its status
+ * registers HFS1-6 as ramstage reads them at BS_DEV_INIT, while HECI
+ * (00:16.0) is still visible, and the me_disable option.
+ */
+struct mb_me_status {
+	bool valid;
+	uint32_t hfs[6];
+	unsigned int me_disable;
+};
+
+const struct mb_me_status *mainboard_me_status(void);
+
+/*
+ * One of "Disabled (AltMeDisable, BUP)", "Stopped in BUP (state 0xNN)",
+ * "Disabled (soft temporary disable)", "Enabled", "Enabled, not ready (state
+ * N)", "Security override (jumper)", "Security override (HECI message)",
+ * "Debug", "Mode N" and "Not available"
+ */
+const char *mainboard_me_summary(void);
+
+/* The help text of the setup: registers, numbers, HECI */
+const char *mainboard_me_details(void);
+
+#endif /* MAINBOARD_LENOVO_HASWELL_ME_STATUS_H */
diff --git a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/cfr.h b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/cfr.h
index fef850cc1a..4131822694 100644
--- a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/cfr.h
+++ b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/cfr.h
@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@ static const struct sm_object me_disable = SM_DECLARE_ENUM({
 	.opt_name	= "me_disable",
 	.ui_name	= "Intel ME interface (HECI)",
 	.ui_helptext	= "The PCI interface (HECI) of the Management Engine, through\n"
-			  "which the OS talks to it. The ME itself keeps running.\n"
+			  "which the OS talks to it. It does not change the ME itself.\n"
 			  "Default: " ME_PCI_DEFAULT ".",
 	.default_value	= CONFIG(DISABLE_ME_PCI),
 	.values		= (const struct sm_enum_value[]) {
-- 
2.47.3

